    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for grub2",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for grub2 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-97876: Bypass of GRUB lockdown restriction in Secure Boot mode via\n  serial command MMIO base address (bsc#1284208).\n- CVE-2026-109906: Fix UUID pointer length mismatch, Fix Use-After-Free in the\n  OOM error cleanup and return path (bsc#1284765).\n- CVE-2026-109907: Fix allocation failure handling in insert_dir (bsc#1284765).\n\nBug fixes:\n\n- Fix memory leak in error path, add missing error return check in\n  grub_initrd_component(), ensure NULL check before memset() in\n  grub_cryptokey_discard() (bsc#1284464).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SLE-Micro-6.0-963",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
